# Privacy Policy

**Effective Date:** 17 September 2026 (replaces the policy dated 4 June 2025)
**App Name:** EduCalling
**Developer:** Project 2morrow Software Limited
**Contact:** info@p2msoft.com

EduCalling is a school management application used by teachers, school staff and guardians. This Privacy Policy explains what information the app handles, why, and how it is protected.

---

## 1. Who Creates Accounts

EduCalling does not let anyone create an account from the app. Accounts are created by the school's administrator on the EduCalling web platform. The app only signs you in to an account that already exists.

---

## 2. Information the App Collects

### When you sign in
- Email address or phone number (your login ID)
- Password (sent to our server for verification only; never stored in the app)

### Information linked to your account
Depending on your role, the school's records that the app shows you include:

- **Guardians:** full name, phone number, email address, and the profile, fee and attendance records of the students linked to you
- **Teachers and staff:** full name, phone number, email address, and the academic, attendance, fee and salary records you are authorised to manage

This information is entered and maintained by the school, not collected from you by the app, except for the login details above.

### Information you choose to upload
- **Leave applications:** guardians may attach documents (PDF or image files) to a student's leave request. These files are uploaded to our server and stored with the leave request. Attaching a file is optional.
- **Records you enter:** teachers may record attendance, exam results, assignments, fee entries and similar school data as part of their work.

### Information we do not collect
- No precise or approximate location
- No advertising identifiers, and no advertising or analytics SDKs
- No contacts, photos, camera or microphone access
- No payment card or mobile-banking details (see section 5)

---

## 3. Permissions the App Requests

- `INTERNET` and `ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE` — to communicate with the school server and to detect when the device is offline.
- `READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` / `WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` (Android 9 and earlier only) — to save fee receipts and reports you download. On newer Android versions no storage permission is needed.
- Files for leave applications are chosen through the Android system file picker; the app only receives the files you select.

Permissions are used only for the action you start (for example, downloading a receipt).

---

## 4. How the App Uses Your Data

- To sign you in and show the records that belong to your role and school
- To let teachers manage attendance, exams, assignments, schedules, fees and salary records
- To let guardians view fees, pay fees, apply for student leave, submit waiver applications and send feedback
- To keep the app usable without a network connection (see section 6)

---

## 5. Payments

Fee payments are processed by a licensed third-party payment gateway. When you choose to pay, the app opens the gateway's secure page; card or mobile-banking details are entered there and are handled under the gateway's own privacy policy. EduCalling only receives confirmation of whether a payment succeeded.

---

## 6. Data Stored on Your Device

To work on poor or absent networks the app keeps a copy of recently viewed records (for example your dashboard, fee summary or class lists) and any changes you saved while offline on your device, in the app's private storage that other apps cannot read. Your login token is kept in the device's secure keystore. All of this is removed when you sign out or uninstall the app.

---

## 7. Data Sharing

We do not sell, rent or share your personal data with third parties for their own use. Data is accessible only to:

- Your school's authorised administrators and staff, according to their roles
- Our hosting and infrastructure providers, who process it on our behalf
- The payment gateway, only for a payment you initiate (section 5)
- Authorities, where required by law

---

## 8. Data Security

All communication between the app and our servers is encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS). Access is role-based and every request is authenticated. Sessions expire automatically, and signing out clears all locally stored data.

---

## 9. Data Retention and Deletion

School records are kept for as long as your school uses EduCalling and as required by its academic and financial record-keeping obligations. You can ask for your personal data to be corrected or deleted by contacting your school administrator or by emailing **info@p2msoft.com** from your registered email or phone number. Fee and payment records may be retained where a legal or accounting requirement applies; we will tell you what has been deleted and what must be kept.

---

## 10. Children's Privacy

Student information is entered by the school and viewed through guardian and teacher accounts. The app does not collect data directly from children and does not provide accounts to them.

---

